WEBVTT

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:03.619
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:06.000
Being together like this...

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.875
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:13.376
Forever...

00:00:13.376 --> 00:00:15.798
...under this sky...

00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:18.092
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.815 --> 00:00:21.070
In this beauty...

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.217
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.264
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.264 --> 00:00:24.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:26.017
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:27.101
...and more loving...

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:28.185
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:29.395
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.646
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.065
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.735
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.945
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.945 --> 00:00:40.656
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.656 --> 00:00:42.700
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.411
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:47.538
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.538 --> 00:00:50.624
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:56.464
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.464 --> 00:00:58.799
If you go there...

00:00:58.799 --> 00:01:02.803
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.803 --> 00:01:06.182
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:08.642
Under this sky...

00:01:08.642 --> 00:01:11.020
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.067
Being together like this...

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.570
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.785
Under this sky...

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.037
...we'll walk together!

00:01:57.741 --> 00:01:58.742
Wait!

00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:01.912
Kyuu's so full of energy.

00:02:02.871 --> 00:02:04.623
On a completely different note, it's really hot.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.836
I thought we'd have normal classes for a while, since we just solved that case.

00:02:10.545 --> 00:02:12.964
I wasn't made for fieldwork.

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:16.968
It's important to learn while
breathing fresh air, too.

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:20.221
What's wrong?

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:27.395
Police cars.

00:02:27.854 --> 00:02:29.356
In the middle of the mountains?

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:33.902
Let's go take a look!

00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:45.455
What happened?

00:02:45.956 --> 00:02:47.332
Apparently it's a murder case.

00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:48.708
How scary.

00:02:48.875 --> 00:02:49.834
Yeah...

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:03.723
What's with this?

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:07.894
Maybe he was killed as he was about to eat.

00:03:09.104 --> 00:03:14.442
I never thought that people from DDS would
come to a remote place like this.

00:03:15.276 --> 00:03:19.239
The victim is 46-year-old Johnson
Itsuki, a food connoisseur.

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:23.326
As you can see, it looks like
he was strangled to death.

00:03:31.001 --> 00:03:33.586
It looks like it's been two or
three days since he died.

00:03:33.753 --> 00:03:34.587
Er, yes.

00:03:34.921 --> 00:03:38.633
Today is Saturday, so that means he was
killed on either Wednesday or Thursday.

00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:39.551
Yes.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.474
...these dishes are no more than half a day old.

00:03:47.851 --> 00:03:49.936
You're right, the soup hasn't congealed yet.

00:03:50.061 --> 00:03:54.733
So, does that mean that the perpetrator came
here again yesterday, just to make these dishes?

00:03:55.025 --> 00:03:55.942
Is that right?

00:03:56.735 --> 00:03:57.819
Why would he do something like that?

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:02.032
This means the perpetrator
has quite a bizarre hobby.

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:07.829
Yeah, killing a food-connoisseur
like him probably means...

00:04:08.705 --> 00:04:12.042
...the perpetrator had a deeply
rooted hatred for the victim...

00:04:13.001 --> 00:04:15.795
...or that he has some mental issues.

00:04:16.629 --> 00:04:19.424
In any case, look at these fancy dishes.

00:04:22.427 --> 00:04:24.721
I'm going to attend the autopsy.

00:04:24.804 --> 00:04:26.222
Then we'll get some work done, too.

00:04:26.806 --> 00:04:28.600
Uhm, who first discovered the body?

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.602
Ah, in the next room.

00:04:32.353 --> 00:04:33.188
Excuse us.

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:41.654
There are four people who
first discovered the body?

00:04:42.739 --> 00:04:46.868
Apparently, these four are the
only ones who knew that...

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.954
...the victim was living and working
in this summer house.

00:04:51.664 --> 00:04:52.916
We're from DDS.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.752
May we ask you a few questions?

00:04:59.339 --> 00:05:05.303
I'm the caretaker of this place,
but I hardly saw Mr. Itsuki.

00:05:06.304 --> 00:05:09.599
I mean, I only bring foodstuffs up
here every Saturday morning.

00:05:10.141 --> 00:05:10.934
Foodstuffs?

00:05:11.559 --> 00:05:15.396
Yes, all sorts of things, fresh
meats, vegetables, eggs...

00:05:17.315 --> 00:05:18.399
That's why I came here this morning...

00:05:28.743 --> 00:05:30.203
Looks like today will be another hot day.

00:05:30.286 --> 00:05:31.329
Mr. Itsuki!

00:05:31.329 --> 00:05:32.372
Open up!

00:05:32.372 --> 00:05:32.997
Sir!

00:05:33.164 --> 00:05:35.375
Mr. Itsuki, please get up already.

00:05:37.544 --> 00:05:38.294
What's the matter?

00:05:39.045 --> 00:05:41.047
He's not coming out, no matter
how much we call him.

00:05:42.882 --> 00:05:44.592
Don't you think that's a bit strange?

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:45.593
Yeah...

00:05:47.011 --> 00:05:48.763
Was I here on Wednesday or Thursday?

00:05:49.556 --> 00:05:53.351
I wouldn't dare; I might disturb him if I
came on a day other than Saturday...

00:05:53.977 --> 00:05:55.353
...so I don't even come close.

00:05:59.399 --> 00:06:00.483
Yeah, that's correct.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.068
I've been here once before.

00:06:02.819 --> 00:06:05.321
I think it was Wednesday afternoon.

00:06:05.738 --> 00:06:06.406
Wednesday?

00:06:06.781 --> 00:06:11.119
Mr. Itsuki was a regular on our gourmet show.

00:06:12.078 --> 00:06:16.166
And I... just wanted to have a meeting...

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:19.919
Mr. ltsuki!

00:06:20.587 --> 00:06:21.588
It's me, Oomuro.

00:06:21.921 --> 00:06:22.881
Are you out?

00:06:28.011 --> 00:06:32.765
That's when this nice coffee scent
waited out from inside.

00:06:33.683 --> 00:06:37.729
So I thought that he might be
engrossed in his manuscript.

00:06:38.855 --> 00:06:39.898
I guess I'll come back later.

00:06:42.942 --> 00:06:47.155
So that means you haven't seen Mr. Itsuki directly?

00:06:47.572 --> 00:06:48.364
No...

00:06:48.823 --> 00:06:53.328
It's kind of weird to come all the way out
here and go home without seeing him.

00:06:53.661 --> 00:06:54.871
Well...

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:03.087
To be honest I came to apologize because we
decided to cut Mr. Itsuki‘s portion of the show.

00:07:04.005 --> 00:07:05.256
I was uncomfortable.

00:07:05.423 --> 00:07:07.842
I see, I guess that makes sense.

00:07:08.259 --> 00:07:11.387
Oh, I'll tell you right now, I didn't kill anyone.

00:07:12.263 --> 00:07:14.474
I think the one that's suspicious
is probably Chizuko.

00:07:15.016 --> 00:07:16.184
You mean that woman?

00:07:16.392 --> 00:07:18.645
Yeah, she's Mr. Itsuki's wife.

00:07:20.063 --> 00:07:23.983
I heard that they're in the middle of
really ugly divorce negotiations.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.151
It's just a rumor though.

00:07:29.322 --> 00:07:32.075
That Kansai-ben producer
really gets on my nerves.

00:07:32.659 --> 00:07:34.827
Spreading rumors about us.

00:07:35.161 --> 00:07:38.331
However, isn't it true that you were in
the middle of divorce negotiations?

00:07:38.873 --> 00:07:40.750
Something about the consolation money...

00:07:43.336 --> 00:07:44.671
Then, I'll ask you something else:

00:07:45.588 --> 00:07:47.799
When did you come here?

00:07:49.509 --> 00:07:50.551
The day it was raining.

00:07:58.351 --> 00:08:00.228
Hey, open up!

00:08:00.937 --> 00:08:03.815
Talking to your attorney doesn't
get me anywhere!

00:08:04.524 --> 00:08:08.069
I'm getting soaked out here. Hurry up!

00:08:11.239 --> 00:08:12.949
I know you're in there!

00:08:15.576 --> 00:08:17.203
Alright, if that's how you want to play it...

00:08:18.162 --> 00:08:20.456
He pretended to be out because he knew
that it would be a bother to see me.

00:08:20.748 --> 00:08:21.833
I'm sure that was his reasoning.

00:08:23.126 --> 00:08:23.918
And after that?

00:08:24.294 --> 00:08:27.880
The rain was getting stronger, so
I went straight back to the hotel.

00:08:28.881 --> 00:08:31.301
And, like I feared, a huge lightning bolt struck...

00:08:31.301 --> 00:08:33.761
...and tripped the circuit breaker
causing quite a ruckus.

00:08:34.679 --> 00:08:35.888
But that's enough, right?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.724
Can I ask just one more thing?

00:08:39.809 --> 00:08:42.645
Is there anything you know about the other three?

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:44.272
Not really...

00:08:45.106 --> 00:08:50.320
Oh, I met that editor, Akai or something,
in the hotel lobby.

00:08:50.737 --> 00:08:51.779
Mr. Akai?

00:08:52.155 --> 00:08:56.868
Yes. He said, "I just went to see him
and he was asleep, snoring.“

00:08:57.368 --> 00:09:00.163
Snoring, was he?

00:09:02.415 --> 00:09:03.708
Yes, that's right.

00:09:04.542 --> 00:09:07.712
I did come here early in the morning that day.

00:09:08.296 --> 00:09:10.590
We were told that Mr. Itsuki was still asleep:..

00:09:11.632 --> 00:09:12.175
Yes.

00:09:16.137 --> 00:09:18.806
I'm sorry to disturb you this early
in the morning, it's me, Akai.

00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:24.145
Mr. Itsuki writes the manuscript for
a cooking manga in our magazine.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.440
The deadline for the manuscript was coming
up, so I wanted to get it right away.

00:09:29.859 --> 00:09:34.238
That's when I heard his loud snoring.

00:09:35.615 --> 00:09:40.370
I thought it'd be bad to wake him
up, so I went back to the hotel.

00:09:41.204 --> 00:09:44.499
That's when I ran into his wife.

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:46.667
I see.

00:09:47.919 --> 00:09:49.670
But, it's horrible.

00:09:51.255 --> 00:09:53.257
Who would do such a thing?

00:09:57.678 --> 00:10:00.765
Did you figure something out, super detectives?

00:10:02.308 --> 00:10:04.185
It's all getting messy...

00:10:04.227 --> 00:10:05.520
Judging from the circumstances...

00:10:05.603 --> 00:10:08.481
...there's still a chance that an unrelated
person is the perpetrator.

00:10:08.648 --> 00:10:11.150
Oh, that's right, I'd forgotten.

00:10:11.651 --> 00:10:14.987
That leaves the collection
of eyewitness statements.

00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:18.950
But we're all the way in the mountains, I don't
think that we can expect a lot of relevant ones.

00:10:20.576 --> 00:10:21.577
That won't be necessary.

00:10:23.079 --> 00:10:26.124
I think that we can safely assume that
the perpetrator is one of the four.

00:10:26.958 --> 00:10:31.462
And to complicate the investigation, the
culprit has made a false statement.

00:10:32.004 --> 00:10:33.714
One of the four?

00:10:33.798 --> 00:10:36.300
Wait, how can you be so sure?

00:10:36.551 --> 00:10:37.552
Yeah, how come?

00:10:38.094 --> 00:10:39.262
Why do you think so?

00:10:44.725 --> 00:10:45.393
What a weirdo.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:51.149
In any case, there should be
a hint that we can figure out.

00:10:51.941 --> 00:10:53.734
We have to find it first!

00:11:00.032 --> 00:11:03.119
Hey, Kyuu, is this the way
to figure something out?

00:11:03.536 --> 00:11:06.956
I feel the hint to solving this puzzle
has something to do with cooking.

00:11:07.665 --> 00:11:10.585
But I don't know anything about French cuisine...

00:11:10.751 --> 00:11:12.795
Just looking at these is making me hungry.

00:11:15.631 --> 00:11:17.592
Hey Kazuma, can I ask you something?

00:11:17.842 --> 00:11:19.093
Sure, ask anything you want.

00:11:21.762 --> 00:11:23.473
what are these black beady things?

00:11:24.307 --> 00:11:27.852
You don't even know what caviar is?

00:11:28.227 --> 00:11:29.395
I didn't know, either.

00:11:29.645 --> 00:11:30.438
Geez.

00:11:30.605 --> 00:11:31.981
Everybody, come quickly.

00:11:35.651 --> 00:11:36.235
What's wrong?

00:11:37.195 --> 00:11:39.906
I figured it out, the secret behind these dishes!

00:11:41.532 --> 00:11:42.074
The secret?

00:11:42.492 --> 00:11:43.618
What is it?

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:50.041
I was only looking at these dishes from
this side, so I didn't notice, but...

00:11:51.959 --> 00:11:56.297
...looking from this angle I noticed.

00:11:58.132 --> 00:11:59.175
The hors d'oeuvre...

00:12:00.051 --> 00:12:00.968
the main dish...

00:12:02.136 --> 00:12:02.803
and the soup...

00:12:04.847 --> 00:12:08.684
more all dishes that I saw
in my sister's cookbook!

00:12:10.853 --> 00:12:13.189
There it is, Megu's photographic memory!

00:12:13.731 --> 00:12:15.525
What kind of cookbook was that?

00:12:16.859 --> 00:12:17.818
The book was...

00:12:23.449 --> 00:12:24.158
Chizuko Itsuki!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:25.159
What?

00:12:25.493 --> 00:12:26.744
That means...

00:12:27.245 --> 00:12:29.163
The perpetrator is Chizuko Itsuki.

00:12:29.622 --> 00:12:33.334
And her motive was the most
clear cut of the four, too.

00:12:34.085 --> 00:12:35.419
Yeah, she is pretty suspicious...

00:12:38.047 --> 00:12:39.549
Don't you think it looks a little forced?

00:12:39.882 --> 00:12:42.552
Mrs. Itsuki is a professional food coordinator.

00:12:43.094 --> 00:12:47.723
I'm sure her repertoire is bigger than
just the dishes from her book.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:54.230
Besides, there are still no clues as to why
these dishes are at the murder scene.

00:12:57.483 --> 00:13:01.988
This case looks like someone with
a bizarre hobby purposely...

00:13:02.071 --> 00:13:03.906
...placed the dishes in front of the body...

00:13:04.699 --> 00:13:08.619
...but there's a reason why the perpetrator
had to leave these dishes there.

00:13:10.288 --> 00:13:12.248
What does that mean?

00:13:13.082 --> 00:13:16.627
I'm certain I can determine
the perpetrator and why...

00:13:17.086 --> 00:13:22.091
...the perpetrator had to leave
these Extravagant dishes.

00:13:24.051 --> 00:13:28.431
Actually, among these dishes,
there is a course missing.

00:13:28.848 --> 00:13:30.266
Missing course?!
Missing course?!

00:13:43.101 --> 00:13:44.685
A missing course?

00:13:45.436 --> 00:13:47.396
What's missing?

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:49.565
The salad.

00:13:49.941 --> 00:13:50.817
Salad!
Salad!

00:13:56.405 --> 00:13:58.741
You're right, the only thing missing is the salad.

00:13:58.866 --> 00:13:59.492
Yeah.

00:13:59.742 --> 00:14:01.744
But what does that have to do with the case?

00:14:01.953 --> 00:14:03.412
I don't have a clue.

00:14:09.836 --> 00:14:10.753
Hey, Kyuu!

00:14:15.007 --> 00:14:16.467
Ah, so that's it!

00:14:18.302 --> 00:14:19.303
You figured it out?

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:20.263
Yeah.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.557
"The dead don't eat."

00:14:26.102 --> 00:14:27.145
That's it, isn't it, Ryu?

00:14:28.688 --> 00:14:29.188
Yeah.

00:14:36.946 --> 00:14:39.282
All of the puzzles have been solved.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:47.498
First, the key to solve this puzzle...
That is the victim's time of death.

00:14:49.458 --> 00:14:53.129
Ms. Katagiri, do we have a good
estimate on the time of death?

00:14:53.462 --> 00:14:57.633
The autopsy only revealed that the body's
decay had advanced due to heat.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.594
The time of death was about
two or three days ago.

00:14:59.635 --> 00:15:03.890
In other words, between Wednesday
afternoon and Thursday around noon.

00:15:04.557 --> 00:15:05.141
I see.

00:15:05.433 --> 00:15:09.937
That means that someone could
have done it after we were here.

00:15:10.354 --> 00:15:13.107
This looks like a murder
committed by a freak to me.

00:15:13.733 --> 00:15:22.366
No, that's not the case, because someone in this group gave a false statement.

00:15:25.881 --> 00:15:26.587
That...

00:15:30.374 --> 00:15:30.958
...was you!

00:15:32.543 --> 00:15:34.086
M-Me?

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.756
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:15:38.007 --> 00:15:38.716
Akai did it?

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:39.759
He did?

00:15:40.593 --> 00:15:41.010
Yeah.

00:15:42.261 --> 00:15:45.306
You said that you came here
on Thursday morning.

00:15:46.641 --> 00:15:48.309
But that was a complete lie.

00:15:48.976 --> 00:15:51.270
You really came here Wednesday night.

00:15:51.604 --> 00:15:52.813
What are you talking about?

00:15:53.689 --> 00:15:58.152
When Mrs. Itsuki left, it was raining really hard...

00:15:58.945 --> 00:15:59.570
...and...

00:16:53.457 --> 00:16:55.543
You killed Mr. Itsuki!

00:16:57.003 --> 00:16:59.922
After that, you hurried back to the hotel.

00:17:00.631 --> 00:17:03.592
Luckily for you, nobody saw you leave or return.

00:17:04.885 --> 00:17:06.012
However, on the next day...

00:17:08.389 --> 00:17:10.766
You ran into his wife at the hotel.

00:17:12.476 --> 00:17:16.439
As you were shaken, you told an unnecessary lie.

00:17:18.149 --> 00:17:23.237
You said, "I just went to see him
and he was asleep, snoring."

00:17:24.655 --> 00:17:31.245
I'm sure you didn't think that this lie would cause you all sorts of problems later on.

00:17:32.747 --> 00:17:38.586
You came back later because you were worried
that the body hadn't been found yet.

00:17:51.098 --> 00:17:57.521
That's when you realized that something
unexpected had happened in this house.

00:17:59.607 --> 00:18:00.691
What happened?

00:18:02.151 --> 00:18:03.611
The circuit breaker had tripped.

00:18:05.738 --> 00:18:06.197
Huh?

00:18:07.239 --> 00:18:09.742
Did you forget Mrs. Itsuki's statement?

00:18:10.785 --> 00:18:14.789
A huge lightning bolt struck and tripped the
circuit breaker causing quite a ruckus.

00:18:15.664 --> 00:18:20.336
I see, that lightning bolt had tripped
the circuit breaker here, too!

00:18:22.254 --> 00:18:25.049
You quickly switched the breaker back on...

00:18:26.467 --> 00:18:29.220
...and went around the house to
check for other irregularities.

00:18:35.851 --> 00:18:43.401
That's when you discovered the mountain of
rotting food giving off a horrible stench.

00:18:44.735 --> 00:18:46.070
And if was found like this...

00:18:46.237 --> 00:18:52.034
...it would have been proof that Mr. Itsuki
was murdered before the thunderstorm.

00:18:52.785 --> 00:18:56.163
If he were still alive, naturally he would have
switched the breaker back on immediately...

00:18:56.789 --> 00:18:58.124
...so none of the food would have rotted.

00:19:02.503 --> 00:19:04.338
You must have panicked.

00:19:04.839 --> 00:19:10.511
You had told Mrs. Itsuki that he had
been snoring on Thursday morning.

00:19:11.804 --> 00:19:15.933
It was only a matter of time before someone
would figure out that that was a complete lie.

00:19:18.102 --> 00:19:20.146
There was only one way to cover it up.

00:19:21.814 --> 00:19:24.608
And that was to use up all the rotten foodstuffs.

00:19:25.901 --> 00:19:29.113
But if you had simply thrown it away, the empty
fridge would have caused suspicion.

00:19:30.322 --> 00:19:30.906
Isn't that it?

00:19:31.907 --> 00:19:35.703
If you had restocked it with stuff from another store, the caretaker would have noticed.

00:19:36.704 --> 00:19:40.499
While you were thinking about
this, you got an idea.

00:19:44.003 --> 00:19:51.302
<i>"I know. I'll just use this rotten
foodstuff to make dishes.</i>

00:19:56.223 --> 00:19:57.725
Homemade French Cuisine 2003

00:20:02.271 --> 00:20:05.608
When making the dishes, you stuck
closely to Mrs. Itsuki's cookbook.

00:20:06.734 --> 00:20:11.030
That was because you thought that
you could use her as a scapegoat.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:19.371
That's how you completed your
once-in-a-Lifetime full course meal.

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:26.337
That was quite intelligent of you.

00:20:27.129 --> 00:20:29.673
If you stir-fry things in oil,
boil them, or fry them... ..--

00:20:30.132 --> 00:20:33.385
...someone else couldn't tell that
they were rotten originally.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:39.141
Nobody would be likely to taste any of
the dishes at the scene of a murder.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:40.768
Not to mention...

00:20:41.977 --> 00:20:43.479
"The dead don't eat."

00:20:44.104 --> 00:20:44.563
Yep.

00:20:44.855 --> 00:20:47.608
How did you figure that out?

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:51.320
It's because the salad was missing.

00:20:53.322 --> 00:20:56.825
That was the final hint.

00:20:58.744 --> 00:21:00.663
Even if you could deceive us
with the other ingredients...

00:21:00.913 --> 00:21:03.082
...there is no way you could have
deceived us with salad.

00:21:04.166 --> 00:21:07.169
Salads are made from raw vegetables.

00:21:07.336 --> 00:21:08.379
So that's what happened!

00:21:08.712 --> 00:21:11.340
There's no evidence!
There's no physical evidence!

00:21:11.882 --> 00:21:12.716
Here I am!

00:21:14.802 --> 00:21:18.472
I fi-na-lly found it.

00:21:19.223 --> 00:21:23.978
When I checked all the trash that came from
this summer house at the dump, I found this.

00:21:24.478 --> 00:21:26.689
Rotten kitchen scraps and
Mrs. Itsuki's cook book.

00:21:26.981 --> 00:21:27.690
And...

00:21:28.899 --> 00:21:30.901
Akai, your fingerprints!

00:21:31.443 --> 00:21:32.778
That's our Kinta!

00:21:36.949 --> 00:21:41.495
If that's not enough, just check
the VCR over there.

00:21:43.247 --> 00:21:47.543
It's been reset-- that's the biggest clue
that the circuit breaker was tripped.

00:21:55.342 --> 00:22:00.472
A trivial mistake on my part made him angry.

00:22:02.182 --> 00:22:09.523
He said I shouldn't be in charge anymore
and I completely lost myself.

00:22:13.986 --> 00:22:15.446
We'll hear the rest of this down
at the police station.

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:38.135
Well, let's call it a day here.

00:22:39.178 --> 00:22:42.931
I'll report your success to Headmaster Dan.

00:22:43.682 --> 00:22:45.809
Yay! Please do!

00:22:46.477 --> 00:22:50.272
Though, who would have thought that we‘d
get involved in a case during field work?

00:22:50.481 --> 00:22:51.815
But Ryu's amazing.

00:22:51.815 --> 00:22:53.776
He solved it so easily.

00:22:55.361 --> 00:22:59.073
Wait, did he have it figured out
when he first saw the scene?

00:23:03.535 --> 00:23:04.036
Ryu.

00:23:09.124 --> 00:23:09.708
Mother.

00:23:10.376 --> 00:23:12.294
Oh, someone's here to pick him up.

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:14.505
A Well, I'm off now.

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:18.467
His mom comes all the way
here to pick him up, huh?

00:23:18.884 --> 00:23:21.428
I guess he hasn't quite left the nest yet.

00:23:21.804 --> 00:23:24.598
But his mother is really pretty, wasn't she?

00:23:32.523 --> 00:23:34.358
Good job, Master Ryu.

00:23:35.442 --> 00:23:37.569
Thank you for picking me up, Ms. Yurie.

00:23:45.538 --> 00:23:47.373
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.373 --> 00:23:49.709
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.709 --> 00:23:52.378
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.378 --> 00:23:54.047
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.047 --> 00:23:56.049
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.049 --> 00:23:58.343
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.343 --> 00:24:00.887
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.887 --> 00:24:02.680
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.389 --> 00:24:06.935
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.935 --> 00:24:10.563
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.606 --> 00:24:13.650
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.650 --> 00:24:16.069
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.069 --> 00:24:18.196
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.196 --> 00:24:19.739
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.198 --> 00:24:22.408
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.408 --> 00:24:24.619
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.119 --> 00:24:26.829
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.829 --> 00:24:30.333
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.125 --> 00:24:33.294
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.294 --> 00:24:35.213
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:35.213 --> 00:24:37.590
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.632 --> 00:24:40.426
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:49.060 --> 00:24:50.228
The time limit is one hour.

00:24:51.563 --> 00:24:53.190
An alibi constructed with trains.

00:24:54.149 --> 00:24:58.487
For the crime to become perfect, our statements are essential.

00:24:59.821 --> 00:25:02.699
The competition between us
and the perpetrator is on!

00:25:04.201 --> 00:25:05.118
There's only one answer!

00:25:10.207 --> 00:25:12.042
Mother, huh?

00:25:14.753 --> 00:25:19.549
I bet everybody is busy trying to guess
your age right now, Ms. Yurie.

00:25:20.467 --> 00:25:21.301
Please, stop it.
